Writer: DOCX/RTF table import reads each cell paragraph's style name and property names once.

For every paragraph of a table whose style (or the table defaults) sets paragraph or character properties,
DomainMapperTableHandler::ApplyParagraphPropertiesFromTableStyle asked the paragraph for its style name once per
table style property, rebuilt the list of all ~400 paragraph property names from the property set info, and
SwXParagraph's state check created a cursor (SwPosition + SwPaM, registered in the node) for every one of those
~400 properties. In a 5 MB DOCX with 4400 tables this was 30 % of the import, 3.5 % of it for the style name alone.

Now the style name is read once per paragraph (nothing in the loop changes it), the property names are kept while
the property set info stays the same (it is one static object for all paragraphs), and the state check creates its
cursor only for the three properties that need one (numbering rules, paragraph style, page style). The values
collected and the autostyle applied to each paragraph are unchanged.

Test: CppunitTest_sw_writerfilter_dmapper, CppunitTest_sw_ooxmlimport, CppunitTest_sw_ooxmlexport,
CppunitTest_sw_rtfimport; DOCX->ODT of the upstream sw/qa .docx files gives the same output as before.
